{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_testing_strategy", "label": "Testing Strategy", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Testing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Test Stellar contracts from fastest to slowest: native unit tests, a local Quickstart network, testnet, then fork tests against real ledger state."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_unit_tests", "label": "Unit Tests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Unit testing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Native Rust tests with soroban-sdk testutils, not WASM, so the debugger works. src/test.rs is pulled in with mod test and gated by #![cfg(test)]. Contracts are no_std; tests may use extern crate std. env.register passes constructor args; env.register_at pins an address."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_resource_limits_in_tests", "label": "Test Resource Limits", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Unit testing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Since SDK 25, Env::default() applies mainnet CPU and memory limits, so a production budget failure fails the unit test. cost_estimate().disable_resource_limits() turns that off; cost_estimate().resources() reads consumption."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_mock_auths", "label": "mock_auths", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Authorization", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "mock_all_auths approves everything and can hide a missing require_auth. Pair it with env.auths(), or approve one invocation with MockAuth and MockAuthInvoke. env.auths() is only the latest invocation and resets on the next client call, so assert immediately and check the exact tree on security-critical paths. Use mock_all_auths_allowing_non_root_auth() when the contract authorizes calls below the entry point."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_ledger_time", "label": "Ledger Time in Tests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Time and ledger state", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "env.ledger().set_timestamp and set_sequence_number drive vesting and timelock tests."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_event_assertions", "label": "Event Assertions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Events", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A #[contractevent] struct compares to emitted XDR. events().all() is only the latest invocation. event.to_xdr(&env, &contract_id) builds the expected ContractEvent."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_storage_ttl_tests", "label": "Storage TTL Tests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Storage TTL", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "get_ttl lives on the testutils storage traits, such as Persistent, and is read inside env.as_contract."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_cross_contract_tests", "label": "Cross-Contract Tests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Cross-contract", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Register a real dependency from its WASM with contractimport and env.register(token::WASM), then drive both contracts through typed clients."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_stellar_quickstart", "label": "Stellar Quickstart", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Local network", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "stellar container start local, or the stellar/quickstart image, serves RPC at http://localhost:8000/soroban/rpc and Horizon at http://localhost:8000. The passphrase is Standalone Network ; February 2017."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_testnet", "label": "Testnet", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Testnet", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Public rehearsal network. RPC is https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org, Horizon is https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org, and the passphrase is Test SDF Network ; September 2015. Testnet resets quarterly, so script deploys and do not treat its state as durable. It runs the next protocol before mainnet."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_friendbot", "label": "Friendbot", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Testnet", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "https://friendbot.stellar.org funds testnet accounts. It does not exist on mainnet."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_integration_tests", "label": "Integration Tests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Integration tests", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TypeScript tests against local or testnet follow the frontend flow: simulate, assemble, sign, and send. In Rust, gate network tests with #[ignore] and run cargo test -- --ignored when the network is up."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_stellar_sdk", "label": "@stellar/stellar-sdk", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Integration tests", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JavaScript SDK used to build, simulate, assemble, sign, and submit contract transactions."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_fuzzing", "label": "Fuzzing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Fuzz testing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every #[contracttype] implements SorobanArbitrary when testutils is on, so cargo-fuzz works without extra derives. The lib plus cdylib crate types already expose the lib target. Call try_ methods so an unexpected panic fails the target. Run with cargo +nightly fuzz run."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_soroban_arbitrary", "label": "SorobanArbitrary", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Fuzz testing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Arbitrary impl for #[contracttype] values, enabled by the testutils feature. proptest uses the same trait."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_soroban_token_fuzzer", "label": "soroban-token-fuzzer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Fuzz testing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reusable cargo-fuzz harness for token contracts."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_property_tests", "label": "Property-Based Testing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Property-based testing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "proptest plus SorobanArbitrary runs in ordinary cargo test and locks in invariants found by fuzzing. Fuzz to find the bug, then keep a proptest regression in CI."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_test_snapshots", "label": "Test Snapshots", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Snapshots, fork tests, mutation tests", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each test writes events and final ledger state as JSON under test_snapshots/. Commit the files so a diff shows unintended behavior. Env::new_with_config can turn snapshots off."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_fork_tests", "label": "Fork Tests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Snapshots, fork tests, mutation tests", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "stellar snapshot create writes ledger JSON, and Env::from_ledger_snapshot_file replays tests against it. For an upgrade rehearsal, stellar contract fetch pulls the deployed WASM so the old and new versions can be compared."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_mutation_tests", "label": "Mutation Testing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Snapshots, fork tests, mutation tests", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "cargo-mutants edits source and reports MISSED where the suite did not notice."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_resource_profiling", "label": "Resource Profiling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Resource profiling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "stellar contract invoke --send=no reports CPU instructions, ledger reads and writes, and fees without submitting. env.cost_estimate().resources() reports the same numbers in unit tests."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_ci", "label": "Contract CI", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "CI", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On push and pull request: stable Rust, rustup target add wasm32v1-none, cargo test, and a release build for wasm32v1-none. Integration jobs run stellar/quickstart and install stellar-cli with cargo install --locked."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_testing_strategy", "target": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_skill_stellar_smart_contracts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Testing", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_testing_strategy", "target": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_development_development_patterns", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Testing", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_testing_strategy", "target": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_security_review", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Testing", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_testing_unit_tests", "target": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_skill_testutils", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/testing.md", "source_location": "Unit testing", "we